PegResponsiveIrm::previewBorrowRate()
├── given the configured oracle cannot produce ABI-decodable return data
│   ├── when oracle is a non-contract address
│   │   └── it should revert when caller-side ABI decoding receives empty return data outside the catch
│   ├── when getPrice returns short data, an invalid bool encoding, or a uint48 word with dirty high bits
│   │   └── it should revert because caller-side ABI decoding is outside the catch
│   └── it should leave the complete IRState unchanged and emit no events
├── given an oracle contract getPrice call reverts
│   ├── it should catch the oracle revert
│   ├── it should return priceWad zero, observedAt zero, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   ├── it should not evaluate a prospective stress transition
│   └── it should leave the complete IRState unchanged and emit no events
├── given the oracle call returns successfully
│   ├── when valid is false
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad zero, the supplied observedAt, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   │   └── it should reject before relying on price or timestamp metadata
│   ├── when valid is true and priceWad is zero
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad zero, the supplied observedAt, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   │   └── it should reject before relying on timestamp metadata
│   ├── when valid is true, priceWad is non-zero and observedAt is zero
│   │   └── it should return priceWad zero, observedAt zero, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   ├── when observedAt is greater than block.timestamp
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad zero, the future observedAt, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   │   └── it should reject before subtracting the timestamp
│   ├── when observation age is greater than maxOracleAge
│   │   └── it should return priceWad zero, the stale observedAt, oracleValid false and the stored borrowRate
│   ├── when observation age equals maxOracleAge
│   │   └── it should accept the observation as fresh
│   ├── when observedAt equals block.timestamp
│   │   └── it should accept the zero-age observation as fresh
│   └── when priceWad is type(uint256).max with valid fresh metadata
│       └── it should accept the healthy raw-curve price while leaving the effective preview subject to stress recovery hysteresis
├── given the observation is unusable after a successful or caught oracle call
│   ├── when recovery confirmation is active
│   │   └── it should not actually clear recoveryStartedAt
│   ├── when stressMode is either false or true
│   │   └── it should return the stored borrowRate without applying the raw target or stress floor
│   ├── when block.timestamp exceeds type(uint48).max and a stressed state would otherwise start recovery
│   │   └── it should still return normally because invalidity exits before the timestamp cast
│   └── it should preserve every state field and emit no events
├── given the observation is valid and stressMode is false
│   ├── when price is below stressPrice
│   │   ├── it should leave the stored stressMode unchanged because preview is non-mutating
│   │   └── it should return the exponential raw target for the price
│   ├── when price equals stressPrice
│   │   ├── it should leave the stored stressMode unchanged because preview is non-mutating
│   │   └── it should return stressRate
│   ├── when stressPrice is less than price and price is less than recoveryPrice
│   │   ├── it should leave the stored stressMode unchanged
│   │   └── it should return the raw interpolated bridge rate
│   └── when price is greater than or equal to recoveryPrice
│       ├── it should leave the stored stressMode unchanged
│       └── it should return baseRate
├── given the observation is valid and stressMode is true
│   ├── when price is below recoveryPrice
│   │   ├── when recoveryStartedAt is non-zero
│   │   │   └── it should leave the active stored recovery timer unchanged because preview is non-mutating
│   │   ├── when price is below stressPrice
│   │   │   └── it should return the exponential raw target because it is greater than or equal to the stress floor
│   │   ├── when price equals stressPrice
│   │   │   └── it should return the raw stressRate because the floor comparison is strict
│   │   └── when stressPrice is less than price and price is less than recoveryPrice
│   │       └── it should return stressRate by flooring a lower raw target when baseRate is less than stressRate and preserving an equal target otherwise
│   └── when price is greater than or equal to recoveryPrice
│       ├── given recoveryStartedAt is zero
│       │   ├── when block.timestamp fits uint48
│       │   │   ├── it should leave stored recoveryStartedAt zero because preview is non-mutating
│       │   │   └── it should return stressRate by flooring baseRate when lower and preserving it when already equal
│       │   └── when block.timestamp is greater than type(uint48).max
│       │       ├── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast(48, block.timestamp)
│       │       └── it should leave state unchanged and emit no events
│       └── given recoveryStartedAt is non-zero
│           ├── given an artificially corrupted or time-rewound state where block.timestamp is less than recoveryStartedAt
│           │   ├── it should revert with arithmetic-underflow panic 0x11
│           │   └── it should leave state unchanged and emit no events
│           ├── when block.timestamp is greater than type(uint48).max with a fresh observation
│           │   ├── it should not downcast block.timestamp because the existing timer bypasses the recovery-start cast
│           │   ├── when elapsed recovery time is less than recoveryDelay
│           │   │   └── it should return stressRate
│           │   └── when elapsed recovery time is at least recoveryDelay
│           │       └── it should return baseRate
│           ├── when elapsed recovery time is recoveryDelay minus one
│           │   ├── it should leave the stored timer and stressMode unchanged
│           │   └── it should return stressRate
│           ├── when elapsed recovery time equals recoveryDelay
│           │   ├── it should leave the stored timer and stressMode unchanged
│           │   └── it should return baseRate
│           └── when elapsed recovery time is greater than recoveryDelay
│               ├── it should leave the stored timer and stressMode unchanged
│               └── it should return baseRate
├── given stressMode is true and the valid raw target equals stressRate because baseRate also equals stressRate
│   └── it should return that raw value without taking the strict less-than floor branch
└── given any successful call with a valid observation
    ├── it should return the exact source priceWad and observedAt with oracleValid true
    ├── it should call getPrice exactly once
    ├── it should not require market binding or caller authorization
    ├── it should not calculate interest or change lastUpdate
    └── it should preserve every state and configuration field and emit no events
